A headerless file's declaration summary includes its multi-line macro calls, printed as their path and `!` like their outline lines. In `long.rs`, a call longer than the 4 KiB the summary parses is cut by the prefix (ADR-024). No line after its first starts at column 0, so the prefix is the whole 4 KiB and ends inside the call; tree-sitter closes the call where the prefix ends, so it is still listed, followed by `...` for the declarations the cut may hide.
